In this lesson, you'll get a quick overview
of the technology we'll be

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.820
using to automate our LLM evals, continuous integration.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.290
We'll discuss what continuous
integration is, why it's important,

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.440
and that will give us a
solid foundation for the

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.640
automated workflows we'll build in
later lessons.

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:16.640
Let's dive in.

7
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:24.060
So what exactly,
continuous integration or CI is a

8
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.360
development practice that
revolves around making

9
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.260
small frequent changes
to your software

10
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.540
and thoroughly testing
those changes with everyone else's. In

11
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.910
other words, you're continuously
validating that your

12
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.970
new features and updates work as
intended when integrated

13
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.520
with those from the rest of
your team. This method

14
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.060
allows you to detect and
fix issues early, before they

15
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.440
become bigger problems
that are harder for you and

16
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.180
your team to solve.

17
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.840
Let's see how this works in
the context of an LLM-powered application.

18
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.320
Imagine you're working on a cutting-edge virtual
assistant application.

19
00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.990
With continuous integration,
every time you or a

20
00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.220
team member makes a code change,
be it refining the LLM prompts

21
00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.030
or updating data integrations,
you merge that change

22
00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.440
into a central repository.

23
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.440
Now here's where the magic happens.

24
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.320
Once the code is merged,
the CI platform kicks in.

25
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.030
It automatically builds your
application, simulating how it would

26
00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.720
behave in a real-world environment.

27
00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.120
Automated tests are run to ensure
that your LLM produces accurate and

28
00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.040
reliable results.

29
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.230
These tests cover
everything from basic

30
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.750
functionality to more
complex issues like

31
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.440
hallucinations or biased outputs.

32
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:33.800
Why is this important?

33
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.500
Well, think of it as
having a supercharged feedback loop.

34
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.500
The CI platform
provides near instantaneous

35
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.940
feedback on your changes.

36
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.280
If an issue is detected,
perhaps the model

37
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.920
is generating unexpected outputs,
you're alerted right away.

38
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.010
This rapid feedback loop
allows you to catch

39
00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.410
and address issues early
in the development cycle. That way,

40
00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.780
buggy code doesn't make its way into
other features your team

41
00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.920
members are building, or
even worse, get

42
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.140
deployed to your users.

43
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.280
Now let's talk about the perks for
you as a developer.

44
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.840
Continuous integration
significantly reduces the time

45
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.800
and effort spent on debugging and
troubleshooting. It's

46
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.760
not that your test will never fail, but
when a test does fail, you'll have

47
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.540
actionable information you can
use to get back on track quickly and

48
00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.640
continue innovating.

49
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.680
CI empowers you to iterate quickly,
experiment with new features,

50
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.140
and make improvements with confidence.
But the advantages

51
00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.820
extend beyond individual developers.

52
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.000
For teams, CI fosters collaboration
by encouraging smaller,

53
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.500
more frequent contributions.

54
00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.300
Conflicting changes are minimized,
making it easier to

55
00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.680
manage and resolve issues.

56
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.430
The shared repository becomes
a reliable source of truth,

57
00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.380
and the automated
testing ensures that

58
00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.660
everyone is building on a stable
foundation.

59
00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.860
This creates a culture of trust,
collaboration,

60
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.180
and faster delivery of high-quality
software.

61
00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.680
Moreover,
continuous integration sets

62
00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.930
the stage for
additional automation in

63
00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.310
how you deploy, monitor,
and retrain your language models,

64
00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:05.680
enabling your team to move towards
a more agile

65
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.180
and responsive development practice.

66
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:11.240
For AI developers,
where innovation is rapid and constant,

67
00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.840
CI provides the structure needed to
excel.

